---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Tabs from '@/components/ui/Tabs.astro';
import Prose from '@/components/Prose.astro';

const tabs = [
  { id: 'five-points', label: '5 Points of Yoga' },
  { id: 'four-paths', label: '4 Paths of Yoga' },
  { id: 'sivananda-class', label: 'Sivananda Yoga Class' },
];
---

<PageLayout
  title="What We Teach"
  lead="A traditional, easy-to-learn system of Hatha Yoga and the philosophy of Vedanta."
  description="The 5 Points of Yoga, the 4 Paths of Yoga, and the structure of a Sivananda yoga class."
  narrow
>
  <Tabs tabs={tabs}>
    <Prose slot="five-points">
      <p>
        Swami Vishnudevananda synthesized the ancient wisdom of yoga into five basic principles that
        can easily be incorporated into one's own lifestyle to provide the foundation for healthy
        living.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Proper Exercise (Asanas)</strong> — Yoga poses help develop a strong, healthy body by
          enhancing flexibility and improving circulation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Proper Breathing (Pranayama)</strong> — Deep, conscious breathing reduces stress and
          increases vitality and mental clarity.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Proper Relaxation (Savasana)</strong> — Helps keep the body from going into overload
          mode, easing worry and fatigue.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Proper Diet (Vegetarian)</strong> — Eating simple, healthy and vegetarian foods that
          are easy to digest has a positive effect on mind, body and the environment.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Positive Thinking (Vedanta) &amp; Meditation (Dhyana)</strong> — The true keys to achieving
          peace of mind and eliminating negativity in our lives.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Prose>

    <Prose slot="four-paths">
      <p>
        The Four Paths of Yoga all lead to the same place — union with the Divine — but help in
        getting there by giving options that fit different human temperaments and approaches to
        life.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Karma Yoga</strong> (the yoga of action) — teaches us to act without egoistic expectations
          in all endeavours of daily life.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bhakti Yoga</strong> (the path of devotion) — for those with an emotional nature who
          enjoy prayer, worship and chanting (kirtan).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Raja Yoga</strong> (the science of the mind) — a comprehensive journey to understanding
          our mind and thoughts through mental control.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Jnana Yoga</strong> (the yoga of knowledge) — for those with strong intellectual tendencies,
          using Vedanta as a vehicle for Self-realization.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Prose>

    <Prose slot="sivananda-class">
      <p>
        A Sivananda yoga class is a traditional class which encourages proper breathing,
        flexibility, strength and vitality in the body while calming the mind.
      </p>
      <p>
        A typical class includes pranayama (breathing exercises), warm-ups including Sun Salutations
        (Surya Namaskar), 12 basic asanas (postures) and deep relaxation. The asanas follow an exact
        order that allows for the systematic movement of every major part of the body in a balanced
        way, helping to enhance prana (life-force energy) and quiet the mind.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>The 12 basic asanas</strong> are much more than just stretching. They open the energy
        channels, chakras and psychic centres of the body while increasing flexibility of the spine, strengthening
        bones, and stimulating the circulatory and immune systems. With regular practice one can increase
        overall physical and mental health and aid in the prevention of diseases such as diabetes, hypertension
        and arthritis.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </Tabs>
</PageLayout>
